{
  "_about": "Gap-filling from public sources. Only U.S. government works (public domain) are used for text; photos come from Wikimedia Commons with their own licenses and credits. Text is never typed here: each field names a source, its PDF pages, and a short 'from' and 'to' phrase, and tools/extract_public_sources.py copies the span between them word for word. Season 'months' are the one editorial choice: they map the source's own timing words (e.g. 'springtime', 'June to September') to calendar months for the 'Right now' note. The source files live in guide-build-kit/sources/public/.",
